caption: Worked Comparisons

Benchmark: assume a target with 100 base HP, an attack doing 20 basic damage, Vulnerability ×2, and compare SPAA 1 with SPAA 100. Ignore ordinary cutting, impaling, or piercing wounding modifiers for this benchmark so only SPA behavior is visible.

No DR: a SPA-scaled attack inflicts 40% of HP at SPAA 1 and 40% at SPAA 100. A mundane bane attack also inflicts 40% at SPAA 1 and, after the Bane Bridge, 40% at SPAA 100.

Applicable innate DR 10 that scales with SPA: a SPA-scaled attack inflicts 20% of HP at SPAA 1 and 20% at SPAA 100. A mundane bane inflicts 20% at SPAA 1 but 0% at SPAA 100 because the SPA-scaled DR stops it before a Bane Bridge can occur.

Innate DR bypassed, mundane worn DR 5: either a SPA-scaled attack or a mundane bane inflicts 30% of HP at SPAA 1. At SPAA 100, the SPA-scaled attack inflicts approximately 40% because the fixed mundane DR is negligible against the already-scaled attack, while the mundane bane still inflicts 30% because the mundane DR is subtracted before its Bane Bridge.

Innate DR bypassed, SPA-scaled worn DR 5: either attack inflicts 30% of HP at SPAA 1. At SPAA 100, the SPA-scaled attack still inflicts 30%, while the mundane bane inflicts 0% because the SPA-scaled armor stops it before the bridge.

Innate DR bypassed, mundane worn DR 5 plus SPA-scaled worn DR 5: either attack inflicts 20% of HP at SPAA 1. At SPAA 100, the SPA-scaled attack inflicts approximately 30% because only the SPA-scaled portion of the mixed armor remains proportionally significant, while the mundane bane inflicts 0% because the SPA-scaled DR layer stops it before the bridge.
